Implemented cutoff-specific temporal transformer campaign scaffolding and persisted the evaluator/input profile.
RepoMemory sections consulted: core.architecture, core.entrypoints, core.where_to_edit, core.invariants, core.testing, core.gotchas, core.dependencies
Implemented the supplied champion reproduction/cache, hosted gpt-5.6-luna structured semantics, hashed-text distillation, causal event-day CSR, 3x160 transformer pretraining objectives, exact cutoff trunks, zero-shot survival, frozen/full heads, forward-fold/bootstrap gates, two-model final lineage, and rank blending.
Fast evaluation passed with the required 30,000-customer, length-16, 300-step debug pipeline and full-shape fallback predictions.
First full attempt stopped after three successful 128-row teacher batches when a later gpt-5.6-luna response omitted requested ids; changed teacher ids to compact sequential values, reduced batches to 64, increased the completion allowance, and retry only missing ids within each batch.
The next full run scored 0.7115937942 but post-run diagnostics exposed an ordering bug: parallel DuckDB split scans had no `file_row_number ORDER BY`, making transformer rows nondeterministic and the internal champion OOF appear at AUC 0.497. Voided run_0002, enforced original row order, versioned every affected seed/fold/final cache, and scheduled a clean remeasurement.
Corrected run_0004 reproduced the champion at ROC-AUC 0.7114786362; the cutoff transformer and its 0.1-0.5 blends failed the 80% paired-support gate, so the legal fallback shipped. A follow-up internal forward-fold test added the retained LLM-distilled semantic summaries directly to the champion feature matrix; the 0.7 semantic-model rank blend improved all three folds to 0.680839/0.701992/0.699667 with median paired support 1.0 and was promoted for remeasurement.
The promoted semantic-champion blend measured 0.7113950723 on run_0006, 0.0000836 below the reproduced champion and far inside the measured 0.000805 validation SE. In accordance with the required champion floor and simple-model tie break, retained its artifacts as a decorrelated finalist but restored the reproduced champion as the shipped fallback.
Auditing the transformer blend gate found a selection bug: it tested bootstrap support only for the highest-median weight (0.3) and discarded the entire grid when that candidate failed. The exact grid gate admits weight 0.2 with fold improvements +0.000303/+0.000194/+0.000813 and bootstrap supports 0.98/0.97/1.00; changed the selector to take the highest-ranked admissible grid point.
Final registered run_0009 measured validation ROC-AUC 0.7120386717, average precision 0.7910460687, accuracy 0.6341265813, and F1 0.6806288076. Prediction contract checks passed on both archived arrays.
Iteration 2 first rescored and banked run_0014 at ROC-AUC 0.7123846047, with byte-matched validation and test copies in the versioned shared cache.
Implemented eight-bucket query-customer-excluded raw and state-residual propagation over causal last 1/4/8 distinct products, category/brand empirical-Bayes shrinkage, undecayed and 730-day half-life accumulators, 33 emitted graph features, and separate legal Model A/Model B final materialization.
Implemented a 64D source-only robust-scaled causal kNN expert using 24 renewal/context scalars, 24 last-product MiniLM components, 16 source-only semantic PCA components, latest matured row per external customer, CPU FAISS IndexIVFPQ, exact customer removal, 512-to-100 retrieval, rate/age/distance/entropy diagnostics, and the 90-minute projection gate.
The kNN expert was rejected after its 0.05 blend moved origins 20/24 by +0.000337/-0.000156. A nonnegative C=0.05 rank stack excluded it, retained a 0.10 graph rank contribution developed on origins 20/24, and confirmed +0.0000125 on origin 30 with 1,000-draw clustered P(improvement)=0.806.
The first complete candidate used a compact renewal graph model and confirmed +0.0000217 on origin 30 but was replaced after broadening the graph consumer to the forward-gated lane-1 representation. A full 372-feature matrix trial was interrupted after matrix construction because projected LightGBM runtime was too high; a source-training-only gain screen reduced it to 96 features.
Official-validation scoring was consulted only after the stack freeze: the final candidate diagnostic moved from run_0014 ROC-AUC 0.7123846047 to 0.7124067197, rank correlation 0.999886, with bootstrap SE 0.0007645.
